Looking at the percentage change in Housing Affordability Index (HAI) which is simply Median Home Price / Median Household Income from 2000 - 2023 This map shows the counties that have a Higher HAI (Red) compared to Lower HAI (Blue)

Counties labelled 1-5 are the top 5 largest increases in HAI over the time period. 

Source: U.S. Census Bureau's American Community Survey (ACS 5-Year Estimates). https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/acs.html

Additionally I have created an interactive map and Data Explorer with 1980 to 2023 Data for both HAI and RAI (Rent Affordability Index - Median Monthly Household Income / Median Gross Total Rent) 

